@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/{id}/publish-to-mail/prepare + /send — owner-signed mail binding
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Team owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.publishToMail(id, req)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> SDK : publishToMail(id, {localPart, mailDomain})

group Phase 1 — prepare (side-effect light: a render plus a uniqueness read)
SDK -> API : POST .../{address}/{id}/publish-to-mail/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare binding
Domain -> Domain : conservative RFC 5321-compatible grammar;\ncanonical form is the lowercase address
alt grammar fails
Domain --> API : 422 {code: invalid_mail_address}
else team unknown under the address
Domain --> API : 404 {code: team_not_found}
else team never deployed (no registry URI to bind)
Domain --> API : 422 {code: team_not_deployed}
else address actively bound to a DIFFERENT team
Domain -> Chain : listChannelBindings("mail") — uniqueness read
Domain --> API : 409 {code: binding_duplicate}
else clear
Domain --> API : PublishToMailResp { address, contract }\n— NO account creation, NO key material\n(mailbox DEKs are the mail bridge's, never embers')
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end
end

group Sign and send
SDK -> SDK : sign with the team owner's wallet key
SDK -> API : POST .../publish-to-mail/send { echo, signed, token }
API -> Domain : deploy signed binding
Domain -> Chain : deploy saveChannelBinding("mail",\naddress, team URI, team_id)
note right of Chain #FFF0C7
Owner-adjudicated: the clause visits the
signer's own team record. Binding key =
channel|address. Re-publishing the same team
reactivates; a different team aborts
"binding address already in use".
end note
alt clause aborts
Chain --> Domain : deploy errored
Domain -> Chain : re-read bindings to name the cause
alt address held by another team
Domain --> API : 409 {code: binding_duplicate}
else signer does not own the team
Domain --> API : 403 {code: binding_unauthorized}
end
else clause lands
Chain --> Domain : finalized; acknowledged
Domain -> Chain : readback: the binding must be observably\nactive before the owner is told the team\nis reachable by mail
Domain --> API : deploy id
API --> SDK : 200 SendResp { deployId }
SDK --> Owner : bound address; the mail bridge's refresh\npicks it up (450 while provisioning the DEK)
end
end
@enduml
